only ever inconvenience the people who intended to pay. The obligation here is
contractual, and it is enforceable in the ordinary way.

Consequently there is nothing to install, nothing to renew, and nothing that can
break in production because a file expired or a server was unreachable.

What a licensee receives is a countersigned agreement, an invoice, and an entry
in PDFluent's licence register. Those are the deliverables.


